1: # Plugin Testing Guide
2: 
3: ## Overview
4: 
5: Flutter plugins require special testing strategies because they include native code. This guide covers testing plugin packages with Dart, native, and integration tests.
6: 
7: ## Test Types for Plugins
8: 
9: | Type           | Tests                      | Runs On         | Purpose                           |
10: |----------------|---------------------------|------------------|-----------------------------------|
11: | Dart Unit      | Single classes/functions  | Dart VM        | Test Dart code in isolation       |
12: | Dart Widget     | UI components             | Test environment | Test widget behavior              |
13: | Dart Integration | Dart + Native bridge     | Device/Emulator | Test full plugin functionality    |
14: | Native Unit     | Native code              | Native test env | Test native code in isolation     |
15: | Native UI       | Native UI + Flutter UI  | Device/Emulator | Test native UI interactions       |
16: 
17: ## Project Structure
18: 
19: ```
20: my_plugin/
21: ├── lib/                    # Dart code
22: │   └── my_plugin.dart
23: ├── android/                 # Android native code
24: │   └── src/test/           # Android unit tests
25: ├── ios/                    # iOS native code
26: ├── example/                 # Example app
27: │   ├── integration_test/      # Integration tests
28: │   ├── ios/RunnerTests/     # iOS tests
29: │   └── lib/
30: ├── test/                    # Dart unit tests
31: │   └── my_plugin_test.dart
32: └── pubspec.yaml
